      "text": "The second import silently overrides the first, so `job_monitor` refers to the IBM Quantum provider version, which expects an `IBMQJob`. This job comes from the local Aer simulator. The generic `qiskit.tools.monitor` version works with any job, so I removed the shadowing import.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit, execute, Aer\n# FIX: duplicate `job_monitor` import from qiskit.providers.ibmq.job shadowed the generic one and expects an IBMQJob, not an Aer job -> removed the shadowing import so the generic qiskit.tools.monitor.job_monitor is used, because it works with any job type\nfrom qiskit.tools.monitor import job_monitor\n\nqc = QuantumCircuit(1, 1)\nqc.h(0)\nqc.measure(0, 0)\n\nbackend = Aer.get_backend('qasm_simulator')\njob = execute(qc, backend)\n\njob_monitor(job)\n\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
